-- title:
--   A supersingular fake elliptic curve over O^{nr}/π
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$ divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra, complete for the ideal $I$ generated by the image of $\pi$, with $I$ maximal, such that every element of $O^{nr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $I$ and every monic polynomial over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $I$. Let $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, namely $a > 0$ or $b > 0$, and for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an order (containing $1$, closed under multiplication, $\mathbb Q$-spanning, finitely generated) and maximal among orders, and let $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ be an order coordinate at $r$: additive, injective, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product on $\mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2}) \oplus \mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2})$ with $\varpi^2 = r$, with image dense modulo every power of $r$, and with first coordinate trace-compatible. Then over the field $O^{nr}/I$ there exist a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$ with $\Lambda$-action (a smooth proper scheme with connected two-dimensional fibres, a commutative relative group law, a $\Lambda$-action by base-preserving endomorphisms compatible with addition, multiplication and reduced traces, together with the level structure data) and a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ at $r$ (a two-dimensional commutative formal group with an action of $\mathbb{W}(\mathbb F_{r^2})$ and a uniformiser series $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi \circ \varpi = [r]$ and $\varpi \circ [\alpha] = [\alpha^{\sigma}] \circ \varpi$) such that $A_0$ is a formal module of $X_0$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, i.e. there are formal coordinates along the identity section identifying the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ and carrying the action of each $m \in \Lambda$ into $[\mathrm{coord}(m)_1] + [\mathrm{coord}(m)_2] \circ \varpi$, and $X_0$ has height $4$, meaning that the kernel of $[r]$ on $X_0$ is a finite projective algebra of rank $r^4$ in every field fibre.
--
--   This produces the supersingular base point of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd comparison: a fake elliptic curve with quaternionic multiplication over the residue field of the completion of the maximal unramified extension, whose formal group is a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ (connected, with no ordinary part, since the quaternion algebra ramifies at $r$). It feeds the construction of fake elliptic curves over the algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ for primes at least $5$.
